on_lapis_lazuli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Two halved river pearls, natural freshwater pearls, on a slab of lapis lazuli. The pearls are about 2.5–3 mm (0.098–0.118 in) in diameter. The growth layers are clearly visible.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATwo_halved_river_pearls%2C_natural_freshwater_pearls_on_lapis_lazuli.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Pearls.jpg/500px-Pearls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Pearls.jpg/500px-Pearls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nuclei from Mikimoto Pearl Island, Toba, Japan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APearls.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}